### Export of ECN Information in IPFIX
* **Presenter:** Shuyang Zheng
* **Slide Deck:** [Export of ECN Information in IPFIX](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-opsawg-export-of-ecn-information-in-ipfix-04)
* **Document:** `draft-ietf-opsawg-ipfix-ecn`
* **Discussion:**
  * Shuyang Zheng presented updates from versions -00 and -01, which added co-authors, updated the scope to explicitly cover classic ECN, L4S, and DC-ECN, added range values to ECN code point Information Elements (IEs), added limitations of MPLS ECN marking per RFC 5129, and included appendix use cases.
  * **Poll 1:** "Should octet counters be added for ECN?"
    * **Results:** yes: 0, no: 1, no_opinion: 6 (total: 56)
  * Benoît Claise and Paul Aitken voiced opposition to adding dedicated per-ECN packet/octet counters, pointing out that IPFIX design conventions derive counters from flow key fields rather than creating technology-specific counters. Paul Aitken questioned whether hardware implementations would actually support such counters.
  * Regarding Accurate ECN (ACE) TCP feedback fields, authors proposed keeping ACE separate from the draft to maintain focus on IP/MPLS ECN field monitoring.

