### YANG deVELopment PrOCProcess and Maintenance (VELOCE)
* **Presenter:** Chen Li
* **Slide Deck:** [YANG deVELopment PrOCEss and maintenance (VELOCE)](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-opsawg-4-yang-development-process-and-maintenance-veloce-00)
* **Document:** `draft-ietf-opsawg-veloce-yang`
* **Discussion:**
  * Chen Li presented updates in version -01, making online validation mandatory, adopting Markdown source files, and splitting the procedure into module creation versus module maintenance sections.
  * The presentation focused on creating a new IANA registry for file indirection and YANG module versions to avoid requiring an RFC publication for every minor YANG revision.
  * Rob Wilton and Mahesh Jethanandani discussed the mechanism: an RFC would contain an indirection pointer to an IANA registry entry, which is updated whenever new module versions are published.
  * Chairs noted that because VELOCE addresses IETF process modifications, a WG recharter may be evaluated. The authors were asked to summarize end-to-end workflows on the mailing list to gather wider feedback.

