### Applying COSE Signatures for YANG Data Provenance
* **Presenter:** Diego Lopez
* **Slide Deck:** [Applying COSE Signatures for YANG Data Provenance](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-opsawg-5-applying-cose-signatures-for-yang-data-provenance-00)
* **Document:** `draft-ietf-opsawg-yang-provenance`
* **Discussion:**
  * Diego Lopez outlined updates addressing Security Directorate feedback, CBOR/SID file assignment decoupling into repository files (allocating 50 SID blocks), counter-signature support, and XML formatting cleanups.
  * Diego clarified the distinction between deterministic encodings (canonicalization) required for wire-level COSE signatures versus broader YANG data store normalization (decoupled into a separate draft).
