### Normalized Representation of YANG Data for Equivalence Evaluation
* **Presenter:** Ana Garcia (Ana Mendez)
* **Slide Deck:** [Normalized Representation of YANG Data for Equivalence Evaluation](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-opsawg-normalized-representation-of-yang-data-for-equivalence-evaluation-01)
* **Document:** `draft-garcia-opsawg-yang-normalization`
* **Discussion:**
  * Derived from the YANG provenance work, this draft proposes building an Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) to enable deterministic byte-level comparison of YANG data across different serializations (XML, JSON, CBOR).
  * Rob Wilton noted that normalization must be schema-dependent to properly handle data types like `identityref` or diffs between JSON and CBOR encodings.
  * Mahesh Jethanandani and Joe Clarke discussed whether NETMOD or OPSAWG is the appropriate home for this work.

