### Ordered Information Element Export in IPFIX
* **Presenter:** Paulo
* **Slide Deck:** [Ordered Information Element Export in IP Flow Information Export (IPFIX)](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-opsawg-9-ordered-information-element-export-in-ip-flow-information-export-ipfix-00)
* **Document:** `draft-heller-opsawg-ordered-ie-ipfix`
* **Discussion:**
  * Paulo presented a mechanism to preserve the order of repeated Information Elements using new IPFIX Set IDs (4 and 5) for ordered data and options, targeting MPLS label stack and multi-layer encapsulation use cases.
  * Discussion centered on whether to support partial collections/indexing versus structured data. Thomas Graf suggested explicit entity signaling for missing layers; Benoît Claise noted hardware export performance concerns with structured data. Leonardo (Cisco) supported the work for resolving tunnel vs. customer traffic ambiguity.
  * **Poll 2:** "Should this document be adopted by opsawg?"
    * **Results:** yes: 12, no: 0, no_opinion: 2 (total: 62)

