### SSH Public Key Distribution via TACACS+
* **Presenter:** Douglas Gash
* **Slide Deck:** [SSH Public Key Distribution via TACACS+](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-opsawg-11-ssh-public-key-distribution-via-tacacs-01)
* **Document:** `draft-gash-opsawg-tacacs-ssh-pubkey`
* **Discussion:**
  * Douglas Gash presented an extension allowing TACACS+ clients acting as SSH servers to pull public keys on demand from a central TACACS+ server.
  * The draft supports RFC 4716 and OpenSSH formats, defines continuation packets (`MORE` status) for multi-key responses, recommends short key caching (5 minutes), and defines local fallback behavior when servers are unreachable.
  * Authors confirmed the draft is ready for a WG adoption call.

